codex
I’m choosing two explicit `for` loops. That keeps all iteration in the supplied fixed semantics, avoids a comprehension’s extra closure/heap machinery, and makes the two loop invariants directly state “accumulator plus the fold over the remaining suffix.” I’m also defining the empty-list case as `0.0`, so the implementation and theorem cover every finite float list instead of silently excluding size zero.
apply patch
