The deviation loop’s arithmetic reached `subF(projectFloat(V), MEAN)`, but lookup of `abs` branched because the invariant allowed an arbitrary module map that could shadow the builtin or make it a closure cell. The actual loaded program’s module scope contains only the target function. I’m tightening both invariants to that exact binding, which preserves Python name-resolution fidelity and removes impossible branches.
